p=page('1. PROJECT SELECTION PHASE','1.1 Software Bid',1);sub(p,'1.1 Software Bid')
text(p,'The Enhanced Personal Finance Analyzer is an academic desktop solution for recording personal income and expenditure, planning category budgets, and tracking savings goals. The proposed benefit is a single local view of manually entered financial activity, with immediate explanatory feedback before an expense is recorded. It does not initiate payments or synchronize bank accounts.',
'The problem is fragmentation of everyday records across cash, digital payment descriptions and informal notes. A monthly total alone does not show which category dominates discretionary spending or how a proposed purchase affects a budget. This project addresses those questions through categorized records, monthly aggregation and transparent financial rules.')
sub(p,'Scope of work and technical approach')
text(p,'The final scope includes local account authentication, transaction maintenance, custom categories, monthly category limits, ratio-based savings allocation, recurring-entry catch-up, charts, text reports, and file transfer functions. JavaFX presents forms and tables; Java services apply validation and calculations; JDBC accesses a local SQLite database. Monetary values use BigDecimal in Java and integer paise in storage.')
table(p,'Feasibility and deliverables',['Aspect','Assessment'],[['Technical','Java 21, JavaFX, Maven and SQLite are identified in pom.xml and source.'],['Operational','Manual entry and local file persistence suit a single-device demonstration.'],['Economic','Dependencies are available without a paid banking API; no measured project cost is claimed.'],['Delivery','Java application, editable report, design diagrams, evidence matrix and test plan.']],[.22,.78])
text(p,'This bid is a retrospective academic statement of the delivered scope, not evidence of a commercial tender, quoted fee or client acceptance. Calendar commitments and role allocations have not been reconstructed without records.')
src(p,'pom.xml','app/MainApp.java:init()','dao/jdbc/DatabaseManager.java:initializeDatabase()')

p=page('1.2 Project Overview','1.2 Project Overview')
text(p,'The application organizes a financial workflow around tracking, planning and analysis. Tracking creates a categorized history. Planning compares actual spending with monthly limits and records progress toward selected goals. Analysis presents aggregate indicators and rule-triggered observations. The user remains responsible for entering accurate records and deciding how to act on the advice.',
'Intended users include students and working individuals who want an offline personal ledger rather than a professional accounting system. Each account has its own user identifier. Shared system categories are available to all accounts, while custom categories belong to a particular user. The desktop stores several accounts locally, although only one account is represented by the current in-memory session at a time.')
sub(p,'Objectives and boundaries')
table(p,'Objectives matched to the final application',['Objective','Implemented mechanism'],[['Record financial activity','Income/Expense model objects; date, category, amount, payment mode and notes.'],['Control spending','Category/month budget comparison and 80%/100% alert levels.'],['Track planned savings','Active goals, target amounts, deadlines and percentage allocations.'],['Reduce missed ledger entries','Recurring rules checked at startup and periodically while running.'],['Explain patterns','Five heuristic rules, category pie chart, three-month bar chart and text report.']],[.31,.69])
text(p,'The system does not include bank synchronization, investment portfolios, tax filing, loan management, email delivery, web access or a remote REST backend. An allocation deposit changes goal balances independently of transaction cashflow. A payment mode is a text description, not a connection to a payment provider.',
'The repository supports a layered, incrementally extensible design. The MST presentation proposed Agile/Scrum and a 14-week plan; no sprint records, interview transcripts or retrospective minutes were provided. That plan is historical intent, not an independently verified development chronology.')
src(p,'model/Income.java','model/Expense.java','service/RecurringScheduler.java','Finance_Analyzer_MST.pptx:slides 2-6')

