p=page('2.4 Software Requirement Specification in IEEE Format','2.4 Purpose and context')
sub(p,'Introduction, purpose and scope')
text(p,'This SRS uses an IEEE 830-style organization: introduction, overall description, specific requirements, external interfaces and verification traceability. It is a structured academic SRS, not a claim of certification against a standard. Its purpose is to specify the delivered local desktop behavior and identify verification gaps before acceptance.',
'The product boundary is one JavaFX application process and its local data files. Its principal functions are manual ledger management, financial planning and interpretable analysis. Requirements below describe implemented behavior unless explicitly labeled target or proposed. Evidence is differentiated as code inspection, executed automated test, historical runtime log or not executed.')
table(p,'Definitions and abbreviations',['Term','Meaning'],[['DAO','Data Access Object: an interface/implementation for persistence operations.'],['JDBC','Java Database Connectivity API used for SQLite SQL access.'],['Paise','One hundredth of a rupee; integer storage unit.'],['Allocation ratio','Integer percentage assigned to an active savings goal.'],['Fixed category','Per-user classification excluded from discretionary concentration/spike advice.'],['Heuristic','Explicit threshold rule; not a machine-learned prediction.'],['FR / EXT / UC / T / A','MST functional requirement / extension / use case / manual test / automated test.']],[.29,.71])
sub(p,'Overall description')
text(p,'The intended user understands dates, categories and monetary amounts but need not know SQL or Java. Java 21 and JavaFX are required for execution. Maven resolves and launches development builds. The data path is relative to the working directory, so demonstrations should launch from the repository root. The desktop and operating-system clock supply dates and recurring scheduling context.')
