p=page('SRS functional requirements for planning and analysis','2.4 Functional requirements FR-05 to FR-08')
table(p,'Planning and analysis requirements',['ID','Required final behavior','Verification'],[['FR-05','Create/edit/delete/toggle goals and distribute positive deposits over active goal ratios. Active total cannot exceed 100 through GoalService.','UC-06; T11-T13; ratio integration tests not run.'],['FR-06','Persist recurring rules with interval/dates/status; generate due occurrences at startup and configured periodic checks; allow manual catch-up.','UC-07; T14; source inspection only.'],['FR-07','Provide an in-modal category budget preview, projected utilization and savings/goal impact before saving.','UC-02; T15; known edit/date limitations.'],['FR-08','Allow recommendation preference changes; produce rule advice and monthly text reports with export.','UC-08; T16-T17; A08-A18 cover rules.']],[.13,.61,.26])
sub(p,'Calculation and timing semantics')
text(p,'FR-05 deposit allocation is a bookkeeping update to goal balances. It neither checks available net income nor debits an account. Independent rounding is a limitation for tiny deposits. Target completion changes a derived progress value, not a stored lifecycle state.',
'FR-06 supports DAILY, WEEKLY, MONTHLY and YEARLY. Periodic checks default to five minutes. The process must be running; startup catch-up iterates missed dates. No exactly-once execution guarantee is asserted because transaction insert, audit insert and next-date update are separate operations.',
'FR-07 is implemented for the current month using an additive proposed amount. A new current-month entry is its reliable intended case. Editing and backdating do not have replacement-aware/date-aware previews. FR-08 report totals use the selected month, but micro-spend advice uses a recent list and today-based window; historical advice therefore has a known period mismatch.')
src(p,'service/RatioAllocationService.java','service/RecurringScheduler.java','service/DefaultInModalAnalyticsService.java','rules/FrequentMicroTransactionsRule.java')

