p=page('SRS interfaces, security and financial logic','2.4 Interfaces and constraints')
sub(p,'External interface requirements')
text(p,'The user interface is local JavaFX: Login/Register, Dashboard, Transactions, Budgets, Savings Goals, Recurring Rules, and Reports & Settings. Modal dialogs collect transaction, budget, goal, allocation and recurring details. No network protocol or REST interface is required. Software interfaces are JDBC, JavaFX lifecycle/events, BCrypt, Java logging and file streams.',
'CSV exchange uses Date,Type,Category,Amount,PaymentMode,Notes with ISO dates and decimal rupee amounts. Imports process one line at a time, skip malformed records, and expose imported/skipped counts. Text reports use a file chooser. Binary snapshots use Java object serialization, contain financial data and a User object including its password hash, and are not encrypted.')
table(p,'Financial logic and acceptance examples',['Operation','Formula / example expectation'],[['Cashflow and rate','Income - expense; (income - expense)/income x 100. INR 50,000 and INR 1,100 imply INR 48,900 and 97.8%.'],['Budget utilization','(spent + proposed expense)/limit x 100. INR 1,000 against INR 1,200 implies about 83.33%.'],['Goal shares','Deposit x ratio/100 rounded to two decimals; 60% of INR 1,000 is INR 600.'],['Concentration','Flexible category amount / (all expenses - fixed expenses); trigger strictly above 40%.'],['Other rules','Expense/income >90%; net savings/income <10%; category growth >=25% with prior >=INR 500; >=5 expenses below INR 200.']],[.27,.73])
text(p,'Security limitations include a plain local SQLite file, a publicly advertised demo account and unrestricted Java snapshot deserialization. Snapshots should be treated as trusted local files. No independent security audit, encrypted storage, remote role management or simultaneous-user isolation guarantee is claimed. Numerical examples above are expected calculations, not database executions.')
