p=page('3. DESIGN PHASE','3.1 Class Diagram',1);sub(p,'3.1 Class Diagram');sub(p,'Case 1 Transaction management')
fig(p,'09_class_transactions','Actual transaction classes, interfaces and dependencies',340)
text(p,'Income and Expense inherit the shared identifiers, amount, date and descriptive fields of abstract Transaction. Their getType() and getSignedAmount() methods supply dynamic behavior. JdbcTransactionDao realizes TransactionDao, whose generic parent contract is Dao<Transaction,Long>. Dashed dependencies indicate service use or object construction, not ownership.',
'Multiplicity between Transaction and Category is a relational identifier reference: each saved transaction has one category_id and a category may classify many transactions. It is not a Java field of type Category. TransactionService validates category existence before saving. Its expense path contains direct JDBC SQL, while its income path calls the DAO interface. The diagram therefore shows both object creation and persistence abstraction without claiming uniform delegation.')
src(p,'model/Transaction.java','model/Income.java','model/Expense.java','dao/TransactionDao.java','service/TransactionService.java')

p=page('Class Diagram case 2','3.1 Budget and savings management')
fig(p,'10_class_planning','Planning services and financial models',410)
text(p,'BudgetService creates monthly Budget objects and delegates storage to BudgetDao. GoalService creates and validates SavingsGoal objects using SavingsGoalDao. RatioAllocationService reads active goals through that interface but executes its allocation batch directly using DatabaseManager. That direct SQL dependency is explained in the component model.',
'The userId fields represent one account to many budgets or goals through foreign keys. User is omitted from this focused service view; no owning List<Budget> or List<SavingsGoal> is present in that Java model. The stored active flag is separate from progress. A goal remains active after reaching its target unless explicitly deactivated. Dashed dependencies indicate service use, not ownership.')
src(p,'model/Budget.java','model/SavingsGoal.java','service/GoalService.java','service/RatioAllocationService.java','dao/SavingsGoalDao.java')

p=page('3.2 Sequence Diagram','3.2 Expense persistence');sub(p,'Case 1 Adding an expense')
fig(p,'11_sequence_expense','Expense validation and JDBC commit sequence',365)
text(p,'The participant named TransactionDialog represents TransactionDialogController. Validators.validateExpense() is invoked by TransactionService; the self-call summarizes a static utility invocation rather than a separate remote component. The JDBC/SQLite participant combines the connection, statement and database for readability.',
'On SQLException the insert path calls rollback() and throws DataAccessException; the dialog catches the exception and keeps the form available. The success result is an Expense with its generated ID. TransactionsController then re-queries the table. Preview queries occur before this save sequence and do not commit a record. No JdbcTransactionDao.save() call is inserted into the expense sequence because it is absent from addExpense().')
src(p,'ui/controllers/TransactionDialogController.java:handleSave()','service/TransactionService.java:addExpense()')

p=page('Sequence Diagram case 2','3.2 Goal creation');sub(p,'Case 2 Creating a savings goal')
fig(p,'12_sequence_goal','Goal validation, ratio check and insertion',365)
text(p,'GoalService validates the proposed fields, reads all active goals and sums allocation ratios before insertion. If the total plus the new ratio exceeds 100, AllocationRatioException is raised before save(). JdbcSavingsGoalDao binds values to INSERT savings_goals and returns the object with a generated identifier.',
'The sequence documents creation only. Funding is a later RatioAllocationService operation, not a side effect of createGoal(). Validation and the sum check are application operations; they are not a database-wide cross-row constraint or a proven concurrent transaction guarantee. The dialog catches ratio errors separately and presents a targeted warning.')
src(p,'ui/controllers/GoalsController.java:handleAddOrEditGoal()','service/GoalService.java:createGoal()','dao/jdbc/JdbcSavingsGoalDao.java:save()')

p=page('3.3 Collaboration Diagram','3.3 Transaction communication');sub(p,'Case 1 Transaction persistence')
fig(p,'13_communication_transaction','Numbered expense-persistence object messages',330)
text(p,'This communication diagram emphasizes object links and numbered messages rather than time-scaled lifelines. Message 1 starts the use case, 1.1 obtains category information, 1.2 validates fields, and 1.3-1.6 perform transactional JDBC work. The dashed return completes the Expense result.',
'The local JDBC Connection and database are represented separately to expose the persistence boundary. prepareStatement() creates a PreparedStatement, which is abbreviated into the connection interaction to avoid overcrowding. executeUpdate() inserts one row; generated-key retrieval assigns the ID. The commit/rollback label represents alternative outcomes and does not imply both execute on success.',
'Income persistence uses transactionDao.save() instead of the direct expense SQL path. The collaboration is intentionally limited to one significant actual scenario rather than merging incompatible alternatives into a single call chain.')
src(p,'service/TransactionService.java:addExpense()','dao/jdbc/DatabaseManager.java:getConnection()')

p=page('Collaboration Diagram case 2','3.3 Recommendation communication');sub(p,'Case 2 Financial recommendation generation')
fig(p,'14_communication_advice','Recommendation engine and rule communication',330)
text(p,'DashboardController queries current and previous spending before passing AnalysisContext to HeuristicEngine. The engine checks the user preference, obtains account-specific fixed-category information through CategoryService, and creates an enriched context using withFixedCategoryData(). It iterates over five Recommendation implementations and collects present Optional<String> messages.',
'Message 1.4* indicates repetition over rules. Each rule can return empty rather than an error when no condition is met. The engine catches exceptions from individual evaluations and logs them; advice from other rules can still be collected. Recommendation has two abstract methods, evaluate() and getRuleName(), so it is not a Java functional interface despite an inaccurate source comment.',
'HighCategorySpendRule and CategorySpikeRule skip fixed categories. Total-expense and savings-rate rules still include fixed obligations. The communication therefore supports explainable advice without suggesting a machine-learning model or external recommendation service.')
src(p,'service/HeuristicEngine.java:generateRecommendations()','rules/Recommendation.java','rules/AnalysisContext.java:withFixedCategoryData()')

p=page('3.4 State Chart Diagrams','3.4 Transaction workflow');sub(p,'Case 1 Transaction dialog lifecycle')
fig(p,'15_state_transaction','Conceptual transaction-dialog states',340)
text(p,'These are conceptual UI workflow states, not values stored in transactions. A new form permits a type choice; an edit form starts from an existing object and disables type controls. Both enter validation on Save. Invalid input or an SQL error leaves the dialog available for correction.',
'Successful persistence closes the dialog and returns saved=true. Cancel closes without a persistence call. A database transaction does not have a stored DRAFT, APPROVED or POSTED status in this schema. Those states would be invented domain behavior and are intentionally absent. The form can mutate an existing in-memory object before a failed update, which is a known implementation boundary rather than a separately persisted state.')
src(p,'ui/controllers/TransactionDialogController.java:showAndWait(),handleSave()','dao/jdbc/DatabaseManager.java:transactions schema')

p=page('State Chart Diagrams case 2','3.4 Savings-goal lifecycle');sub(p,'Case 2 Persisted active status of a goal')
fig(p,'16_state_goal','Savings-goal active flag and deletion',320)
text(p,'The stored state distinction is is_active=1 or is_active=0. A valid creation starts active. Deactivation removes the goal from future allocation; reactivation checks whether its ratio fits within the current active pool. Deletion removes the row rather than changing a status to DELETED.',
'Funding changes saved_paise while retaining the active flag. Reaching the target does not automatically deactivate a goal. getProgressPercentage() derives a percentage and caps its display at 100. A deadline passing is not an implemented EXPIRED transition for SavingsGoal. Recurring rules have a separate ACTIVE/PAUSED/EXPIRED enumeration and must not be confused with goal states.',
'This distinction between persisted state and derived display prevents a common design-document error: representing desirable lifecycle transitions that the application never performs.')
src(p,'service/GoalService.java:toggleGoalActive(),deleteGoal()','model/SavingsGoal.java:getProgressPercentage()','dao/jdbc/JdbcSavingsGoalDao.java:updateActiveStatus()')

p=page('4. IMPLEMENTATION','4.1 Component Diagrams',1);sub(p,'4.1 Component Diagrams')
fig(p,'17_component','Implemented application components and dependencies',340)
text(p,'MainApp constructs DAOs, services, file managers and controllers using constructor injection. JavaFX controllers combine view building and event handling. Services implement business rules, while JDBC DAOs map rows to models. HeuristicEngine coordinates the independent Recommendation implementations. RecurringScheduler owns a single-thread scheduled executor.',
'The component structure is layered but not perfectly strict: DashboardController queries DAOs directly; TransactionService.addExpense() and RatioAllocationService.allocateDeposit() contain direct SQL; MainApp wires file-operation callbacks. These exceptions are visible rather than concealed by an invented web MVC architecture. MainApp.stop() shuts down the scheduler and logger.',
'Java language mechanisms include abstract classes, interfaces, overriding, overloaded constructors/methods, generic DAOs, collections, lambdas, streams, try-with-resources and checked/unchecked exceptions. Transaction.getSignedAmount() is overridden by Income and Expense; AnalysisContext.isFixed(long/String) is an actual overload.')
src(p,'app/MainApp.java:init(),showMainShell(),stop()','model/Transaction.java','rules/AnalysisContext.java')

p=page('4.2 Deployment Diagrams','4.2 Local desktop deployment')
fig(p,'18_deployment','Single-device Java desktop deployment',320)
text(p,'The executable environment is a local Java 21 JVM with JavaFX and JDBC libraries. Maven is a build/launch tool, not a hosted runtime service. The application accesses data/finance.db through a local SQLite JDBC URL and loads app.properties/style.css as resources. File choosers write CSV, text and snapshots to user-selected paths.',
'There is no deployed React frontend, Spring Boot server, REST endpoint, MySQL/PostgreSQL service or cloud component. JavaFX native libraries must match the platform. The repository JAR configuration is not a standalone installer or a verified bundled runtime distribution; the supported development launch path is Maven javafx:run from the repository directory.',
'Because the database path is relative, changing the working directory can select or create a different database. The report build does not launch the app or initialize its database. RecurringScheduler.start() performs immediate catch-up, so capturing future screenshots should use an isolated demonstration copy if existing records must remain unchanged.')
src(p,'pom.xml:javafx-maven-plugin','src/main/resources/app.properties','app/Launcher.java','service/RecurringScheduler.java:start()')

