p=page('5. TESTING','5.1 Test Plan',1);sub(p,'5.1 Test Plan')
text(p,'The test objective is to establish confidence in financial validation, calculation and persistence while distinguishing code inspection from executed behavior. The report preparation compiled production and test sources in a temporary directory and ran only existing database-free tests. It did not initialize or change the production SQLite file. The test run is dated 16 November 2026.',
'The strategy combines white-box inspection of validation/transaction boundaries with boundary-value and equivalence-class tests. Amount classes are null, zero, negative, valid two-decimal and excessive scale. Budget boundaries are below 80%, at 80%, below 100% and at/above 100%. Goal ratios test within and above the 100% active pool. Planned GUI cases cover navigation refresh, type lock, advice toggle and goal-dialog scaling.')
table(p,'Test environment and execution boundaries',['Item','Evidence'],[['Build','Java 21 javac --release 21; 85 production files and 8 test source files compiled in temporary output.'],['Automated execution','18 existing methods in MoneyUtilTest, ValidatorsTest and HeuristicEngineTest; reflective runner invokes @BeforeEach and @Test only.'],['Database integration','Repository classes exist for transactions, budgets, ratio allocation and fixed categories; not executed during this documentation task.'],['GUI / performance / security','Not executed. No response-time benchmark, penetration test, or 100/125/150% scaling result asserted.']],[.25,.75])
text(p,'Entry criteria: source snapshot recorded, dependencies already available, isolated test resources and no production database writes. Exit criteria for this report: compilation evidence, actual automated outcomes, unexecuted cases labeled, and unresolved defects recorded. Exit criteria for final product acceptance additionally require manual screen checks and isolated integration tests; these remain open.',
'Primary risks are accidental startup catch-up writes, incomplete restore, preview inconsistency, tiny-deposit rounding and ordering-sensitive advice tests. Integration and restore testing should use a copied test database with a controlled starting dataset. Peer review is a separate evidence activity and has not been invented.')
